From 2fbfb29fc41dbf1776461b68b80baf48b7b3806f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Lacy <michaeltlacy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 22:50:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 01/11] exemplar-pool: the smell in the kernel's names,
 portable, and loud about gaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The reader's per-token phasepost smell (row.phasepost, from this pool) used the study's older operator names (DES, ALT, SUP) where the kernel has SIG, DEF, EVA, read three absolute paths on one machine, and threw on the first row where the study's data was absent.
- kernelCell(): the study's cell key in the kernel's form ("DES|GROUND" -> "SIG·Ground"); the operator translation is DERIVED from each study operator's own mode and domain (the kernel operator with the same mode and domain), never typed; a gap or a collision is said.
- paths: $EO_LEXICAL_ANALYSIS_DIR, else ~/eo-lexical-analysis; the full centroids through the priors door by name; a missing file is a typed gap in smellStatus(), not a throw.
- smellStatus(): whether the data was found, how many exemplar verbs (at most K per cell: a lookup, not an embedding of the word), the translation, any gap.
The existing exports behave as before (row.phasepost still carries the study's names: reading.js is a baseline-guarded file and its owner decides when to switch); the reading baseline and one-door tests pass. 9 tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
